# .env.telemetry — credentials for the Uptrace telemetry VPS
# Copy to .env.telemetry and fill in your values.
# This file is read by build-deploy-telemetry.sh.

# Required: IP or hostname of the Uptrace VPS
TELEMETRY_SERVER_HOST=

# Optional: domain name for HTTPS (e.g. telemetry.geoconflict.ru).
# When set, nginx + Let's Encrypt are configured on the VPS and the OTLP
# endpoint uses HTTPS. Required for Yandex.Games (game served over HTTPS —
# browser clients cannot POST to plain HTTP due to mixed content policy).
# Prerequisite: DNS A record for this domain must point to TELEMETRY_SERVER_HOST
# BEFORE running build-deploy-telemetry.sh (certbot HTTP-01 challenge needs it).
# TELEMETRY_DOMAIN=telemetry.geoconflict.ru

# SSH auth — standard path:
#   TELEMETRY_SSH_KEY    path to private key (recommended)
TELEMETRY_SSH_KEY=~/.ssh/id_rsa

# Optional: SSH login user (default: root)
# TELEMETRY_SSH_USER=root

# Deprecated emergency fallback only:
# ALLOW_TELEMETRY_SSH_PASSWORD_FALLBACK=1
# TELEMETRY_SSH_PASSWORD=

# Optional: Uptrace credentials (auto-generated if not set)
# Store the generated values here after first deploy so re-runs stay consistent.
# UPTRACE_PROJECT_TOKEN=
# UPTRACE_SECRET_KEY=
# UPTRACE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ── Alert-path liveness probe (task 0284) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Guards the one failure that turns alerting off silently and forever: the profile box's
# alert webhook sits behind an nginx IP allowlist, that allowlist answers 403 on a
# source-IP miss, and a 403 makes the monitoring stack mark its notification channel
# DISABLED with no retry. An hourly cron on this box POSTs a probe to the same URL, with
# the same secret, from the same address a real alert leaves from; the profile box's daily
# checks page through an EXTERNAL dead-man's switch when the probe stops arriving.
#
# Both values are persist-or-reuse on the box: leaving them blank on a redeploy REUSES
# what is already there. To clear one, rm its persist file under /opt/uptrace and redeploy.
# ⚠️ PROFILE_ALERT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN is a SECRET — it belongs in .env.telemetry.secret, not
# here. It is listed here only so the pair is documented in one place.
#
# The full lowercase webhook URL — copy the exact string already pasted into the
# monitoring stack's webhook channel config; do not rebuild it by hand.
# TELEMETRY_ALERT_PROBE_URL=
#
# The shared secret, the SAME value as the profile box's PROFILE_ALERT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN.
# 🚨 NEVER let the box mint this: a token only this box knows is a token the relay does
# not, so every probe fails its secret check and the profile box pages every day.
# ⚠️ It is embedded in a JSON body, so it must contain no " and no \ — hex or plain
# alphanumeric only (it is owner-supplied hex today). ENFORCED: setup-telemetry.sh aborts
# the deploy if the token holds either character, before it touches anything on the box.
# PROFILE_ALERT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=
